  "question": {
    "text": "During an adiabatic process, the pressure of a gas is found to be proportional to the cube of its absolute temperature. The ratio $\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{p}} / \\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{v}}$ for the gas is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{4}{3}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{5}{3}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{P} \\propto \\mathrm{T}^3 \\quad\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_1}{\\mathrm{P}_2}\\right)=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{T}_1}{\\mathrm{~T}_2}\\right)^3$\nComparing it with standard eq. $\\frac{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{p}}}{\\mathrm{C}_{\\mathrm{v}}}=\\gamma=\\frac{3}{2}$"
  }
}